<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Frederick II of Legnica</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1480–1547</span> · Also known as Frederick II of Brzeg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Frederick II of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legnica">Legnica</a> was a Silesian Piast duke who ruled Legnica and from 1521 also <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brzeg">Brzeg</a>. He introduced the Lutheran <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protestant-reformation">Reformation</a> to his duchies in the 1520s and founded a short-lived Protestant university at Legnica. In 1537 he concluded an inheritance treaty with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brandenburg">Brandenburg</a>, later used by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-prussia">Prussia</a> to claim Silesia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/frederick-ii-of-legnica.jpg" alt="Frederick II of Legnica" width="320" height="580" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bartłomiej Strachowski · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fryderyk_II_legnicki.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
